 the runpath value using Msgbox and it seemed all fine. But I don&#39;t understand why this doesn&#39;t work.\nOn a final note, the slave.vbs has SAP GUI automation code and it throws this error when I use HTA to trigger.\n\nC:\\path of slave\\slave_temp.vbs(2, 4) (null): Invalid syntax\n\nBut the file executes properly when the slave_temp.vbs is executed separately. What can be the problem here.?  Does this mean SAP objects don&#39;t have support wen run from HTA ?...\nHelp is much appreciated.\nThe following are the first few lines of the slave_temp.vbs having the SAP automation code\n\nSorry for the long question. But I think the issue is when calling SAP GUI object from HTA. Kindly help me tackle this.\n","excerpt":"the HTA this command is executed to call the slave.vbs\nThis is the command I use to call the slave.vbs\nSet objShell = CreateObject(&quot;WScript.Shell&quot;)\nrunpath = &quot;cmd.exe /K&quot;&amp; Chr(32) &amp;&quot;cd &quot; &amp; Chr(34)&amp;<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> &hellip; &amp;Chr(34)&amp;Chr(32)&amp;Chr(38)&amp;Chr(38)&amp; Chr(32)&amp; &quot;cscript &quot; &amp;Chr(34)&amp;Name1 &amp;&quot;_temp.vbs&quot;&amp;Chr(34)\nobjShell.Run runpath\n\nHere <span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> has the path name and Name1 has the file name of the slave. &hellip; ","title":"Running DOS commands from Vbscript .Help needed with HTA"},{"tags":["python","css","django","internal-server-error"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":63518717,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1688042895,"creation_date":1597996212,"body":"I&#39;m working on a rock, paper, scissors game. I wanted to use a base.html page and extend it with the body of the other pages. It is working for 2 Pages but not for the other two. I can&#39;t find out why i get an Internal Server Error, why my CSS File is not loading.\nHas anyone seen or experienced this before??\n\nMy django views:\n\nUrls.py\n\nThis is my base.html:\n\nthis is my game.html:\n\nbase.css: (borders are only for development)\n\n","excerpt":"static.py&quot;, line 36, in serve\n    fullpath = Path(safe_join(document_root, path))\n  File &quot;D:\\Studium\\it\\repo\\webproject\\yilmaz\\web\\lib\\site-packages\\django\\utils\\_os.py&quot;, line 17, in safe_join\n    <span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> &hellip; ","title":"Django Internal Server Error for only some pages"},{"tags":["aws-code-deploy"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":75162417,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1685230419,"creation_date":1674059697,"body":"I&#39;m having trouble with the AfterInstall hook for CodeDeploy. My code appears to be deploying, however I the AfterInstall script doesn&#39;t appear to be running. I have create a file in  and I set the appspec.yml to execute it\n\nMy afterinstall script is basic:\n\nNo file is being created. CodeDeploy succeeds. If I make the script return false, the step still succeeds and if I provide a location that doesn&#39;t exist, it still succeeds.\nWhere can I get more detailed output or logs for the afterinstall step?\nThis doesn&#39;t appear to contain any useful logs: .\n appears to be empty\n","excerpt":"create a file in data/afterinstall.sh and I set the appspec.yml to execute it\nHooks:\n  AfterInstall:\n    - location: data/afterinstall.sh\n      timeout: 500\n\nMy afterinstall script is basic:\ncd /<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> &hellip; ","title":"CodeDeploy AfterInstall logs"},{"tags":["aws-code-deploy"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":76349423,"is_answered":false,"question_id":75162417,"item_type":"answer","score":2,"last_activity_date":1685230419,"creation_date":1685230419,"body":"As per the the docs, there are two places to look for logs:\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe first is the most useful and should log any errors in your  script. Just look for the lines .\nIn your case it&#39;s most likely a permission issue. Does the user running the  script have permission to write to the  directory?\nIf not, then you need to set the  property in your  file. For example if your web root is owned by ubuntu or ec2-user then run the script as them:\n\n","excerpt":"Does the user running the AfterInstall script have permission to write to the /<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> directory?\nIf not, then you need to set the runas property in your appspec.yml file. &hellip; ","title":"CodeDeploy AfterInstall logs"},{"tags":["reactjs","typescript","git","github-api","http-status-code-422"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":76238914,"is_answered":false,"question_id":76231427,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1683914656,"creation_date":1683914656,"body":"I update the code like your suggestion @AKX but that&#39;s the same error is returned error 422\n\nThe good thing, now the file passed feel good I believe\n\n","excerpt":"}\n      upload_file(git , reader.result);\n    }, false);\n  }\n}\n\nconst upload_file = async (git: { owner: string; repo: string; path: string; token: string | undefined; }, data: any) =&gt; {\n  let <span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> &hellip; = `https://api.github.com/repos/${git.owner}/${git.repo}/contents/${git.path}`;\n  console.log(&quot;data&quot;, data);\n  const res = await fetch(<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>,\n    {\n      method: &quot;PUT&quot;,\n      headers: {\n        Accept &hellip; ","title":"Api github return 422 Unprocessable Enty when the data is passed"},{"tags":["python","tensorflow","keras","conv-neural-network"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":3,"is_answered":false,"question_id":51540068,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1680645242,"creation_date":1532611734,"body":"I am working on an image classification problem with keras and tensorflow. I am using the VGG16 model with Imagenet weights and I am importing my data using the ImageDataGenerator from Keras. \n\nNow I&#39;ve been reading that one should always rescale the images using 1./255 for an efficient tranining. However, once I implement the scaling my model performs significantly worse than before. Changing the learning rate and batch size didn&#39;t help either. \n\nNow I am questioning whether this is possible or if my model has some error. I am using standard .jpg image files. \n\n\n\nModel definition and training\n\n\n","excerpt":"from keras.preprocessing.image import ImageDataGenerator\nIMAGE_SIZE = 224\nBATCH_SIZE = 32\n\nnum_classes = 27\n\nmain_path = &quot;C:/Users/abc/data&quot;\n\n<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> = os.path.join(main_path, &quot;ML_DATA&quot;)\nlabels = listdir &hellip; =True, seed=13,\n                                                     class_mode=&#39;categorical&#39;, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, subset=&quot;training&quot;)\n\nvalidation_generator = data_generator.flow_from_directory(<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> &hellip; ","title":"Keras: Transfer Learning - Image scaling worsens performance of the model significantly"},{"tags":["java","android","filesystems"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":0,"is_answered":false,"question_id":75563484,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1677303148,"creation_date":1677303148,"body":"Im trying to make a custom file system\nim adding new directory by next code:\n\nupon  checker it says that both directory and root file are beign made.\nextracting subderectories with\n\nThis code returns null, even if directories were made by previous code\nI managed to have\n\nWhich mean i probably have permission to create directories.\nI thought it is something about new directories were made and i need permission to access them, tried Intent with ACTION_CREATE_DOCUMENT, but it throws exception\n\nSpent whole night to figure out what is happening, tryied a lot of different solutions, but directory still does not create, or, by some reason, newly made directories are invisible.\n","excerpt":"=fullPath_item+path+&quot;/&quot;+name;\n        File theDir1 = new File(<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>);\n        if (! &hellip; theDir1.exists()){\n            boolean check = theDir1.mkdirs();\n            boolean check2=theDir1.mkdir();\n            //openDirectory(<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>,123);;\n            writeStringAsFile(<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>,&quot;root.txt &hellip; ","title":"new directory made from File not added"},{"tags":["python"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":75404451,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1676018993,"creation_date":1675977101,"body":"I have implemented a Depth-first search algorithm, and using an instance variable called &quot;call-count&quot;, I am trying to track how many recursions/comparisons are executed inside the code, i.e. how many times &quot;searchDFS&quot; is ran. Inside &quot;searchDFS&quot;, the call_count variable defaults to the instance variable the first time searchDFS is ran, then it is passed down through every recursion. All of the other instance variables work fine, I am able to append to the top-level instance array &quot;final_path&quot; just fine, but it refuses to increment call_count.\nWhat am I doing wrong, and is there a better way to do this?\nThe code:\n\n","excerpt":"All of the other instance variables work fine, I am able to append to the top-level instance array &quot;<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span>&quot; just fine, but it refuses to increment call_count. &hellip; =None, visited=None):\n        if(visited == None): visited = self.visited\n        if(<span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> == None): <span class=\"highlight\">final_path</span> = self.final_path\n        if(call_count == None): call_count = self.call_count &hellip; ","title":"Why is this instance variable not incrementing (Python)?"}],"has_more":true,"quota_max":300,"quota_remaining":220}